# {{BRAND_TITLE}} — admin-bff-api (NON-BUILDABLE placeholder skeleton)

> **This is NOT a runnable service.** Base-absent fallback for the mesh
> repo-templating overlay. `snapdragon-admin-bff-api` is a **compiled Spring
> Boot 4 / Java BFF** — unlike the login-ui static bundle it has **no faithful
> minimal boot**, so there is deliberately no vendored source here.

`render_repo_tree()` renders this placeholder only so it never *refuses* when the
Tier-2 base cannot be pulled. **admin-bff-api is effectively overlay-only: the
read-only Tier-2 base (`snapdragon-admin-bff-api` @ the org's GitLab/GitHub) is
REQUIRED to produce a real, buildable tenant tree.**

To emit a real tree, make the base resolvable and re-run:

```
# point at a present read-only clone (never modified, never committed):
ADMIN_BFF_API_BASE_DIR=/path/to/snapdragon-admin-bff-api \
  scripts/render-repo-tree.sh brands/<brand>.conf --enable-repo-tree --repo admin-bff-api
```

The overlay then applies the brand-coupled `application.yml` env-defaults +
`.gitlab-ci.yml` include onto the pulled base. See `../README.md`.
